rm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">fresh or frozen corn kernels</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">unsalted butter</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">honey</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">olive oil</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Salt</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">to taste</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Freshly ground black pepper</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\"> </span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\"> </span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Chopped fresh parsley</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">for garnish (optional)</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-4427-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"4427\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Large skillet&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For sautéing the corn.</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-4427-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-4427-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"4427\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4427-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Heat the Skillet &#8211; Heat the olive oil and butter together in a large skillet over medium heat. Wait until the butter melts and begins to foam.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4427-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Sauté the Corn &#8211; Add the corn kernels to the skillet. Sauté for 5–7 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the corn is tender and lightly browned.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4427-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Add Honey &#8211; Drizzle the honey over the corn. Stir to coat the corn evenly with the sweet goodness.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4427-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Season &#8211; Season the corn with salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste. Mix well to combine.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-4427-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 5: Glaze and Serve &#8211; Cook for an additional 1–2 minutes, allowing the honey to glaze the corn. Remove from heat, garnish with chopped parsley if desired, and serve warm.</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-4427-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>150</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>7g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>3g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>22g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients to make your delicious Honey Butter Skillet Corn!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Honey-Butter-Skillet-Corn.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for Honey Butter Skillet Corn displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-4425\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Honey-Butter-Skillet-Corn.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Ingredients-for-Honey-Butter-Skillet-Corn-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>4 cups</strong> – fresh or frozen <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corn_kernel\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">corn kernels</a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons</strong> – unsalted butter</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 tablespoons</strong> – honey</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon</strong> – olive oil</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Salt</strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Freshly ground <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_pepper\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">black pepper</a></strong> – to taste</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Chopped fresh </strong><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parsley\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>parsley</strong> </a>– for garnish (optional)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-honey-butter-skillet-corn\"><strong>How to Make Honey Butter Skillet Corn</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful Honey Butter Skillet Corn is a quick and easy side dish that will elevate any meal. With a preparation time of just 5 minutes and a cooking time of 10 minutes, you can have this sweet and savory treat ready in no time. Perfect for gatherings or a cozy dinner at home!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Steps-for-Preparing-Honey-Butter-Skillet-Corn.webp\" alt=\"A visual progression for creating Honey Butter Skillet Corn, depicting melting butter, sautéed corn, a honey drizzle, and the beautifully presented final dish.\" class=\"wp-image-4431\" srcset=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Steps-for-Preparing-Honey-Butter-Skillet-Corn.webp 400w, https://www.grandmarecipe.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Steps-for-Preparing-Honey-Butter-Skillet-Corn-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Heat the Skillet</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat the olive oil and butter together in a large skillet over medium heat. Wait until the butter melts and begins to foam.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Sauté the Corn</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add the corn kernels to the skillet. Sauté for 5–7 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the corn is tender and lightly browned.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Add Honey</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Drizzle the honey over the corn. Stir to coat the corn evenly with the sweet goodness.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Season</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Season the corn with salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste. Mix well to combine.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Glaze and Serve</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cook for an additional 1–2 minutes, allowing the honey to glaze the corn. Remove from heat, garnish with chopped parsley if desired, and serve warm.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Side Dish</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>5 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Warm with a sprinkle of parsley</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-honey-butter-skillet-corn\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making Honey Butter Skillet Corn</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use fresh corn for the best flavor and texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Adjust the honey to your taste for sweetness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stir continuously to prevent sticking and ensure even cooking.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a pinch of salt to enhance the sweetness of the honey.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with fresh herbs like parsley for a pop of color and flavor.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-honey-butter-skillet-corn\"><strong>How to Serve this Honey Butter Skillet Corn</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve warm as a delightful side dish at barbecues.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with grilled chicken or roasted vegetables for a colorful plate.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with crumbled feta or goat cheese for a creamy twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix in fresh herbs like cilantro or parsley for added freshness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use as a filling for tacos or burritos for a sweet crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy it as a topping on baked potatoes for a comforting meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve alongside a refreshing salad for a light lunch option.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can easily prepare and store Honey Butter Skillet Corn for later enjoyment:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Honey Butter Skillet Corn Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the corn to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transfer to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refrigerate for up to 3 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing Honey Butter Skillet Corn</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Cool the corn completely before freezing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Portion into freezer-safe bags or containers.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and freeze for up to 3 months.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating Honey Butter Skillet Corn</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight if frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reheat in a skillet over medium heat, stirring occasionally.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of water or broth to maintain moisture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Heat until warmed through, about 5-7 minutes.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What ingredients are needed to make Honey Butter Skillet Corn?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To make Honey Butter Skillet Corn, you will need fresh or frozen corn, unsalted butter, honey, salt, and pepper. You can also add a splash of lemon juice for a bit of brightness! These simple ingredients come together to create a deliciously sweet and savory dish that pairs perfectly with any meal.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. How do you prepare Honey Butter Skillet Corn step by step?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To prepare Honey Butter Skillet Corn, start by melting the butter in a skillet over medium heat. Add the corn and cook for about 5-7 minutes until heated through. Stir in the honey, salt, and pepper, and cook for an additional 2-3 minutes, allowing the flavors to meld. If desired, finish with a squeeze of lemon juice for extra flavor. Serve warm and enjoy!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What variations or add-ins can I include in Honey Butter Skillet Corn?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>There are plenty of ways to customize your Honey Butter Skillet Corn! You can add diced bell peppers, jalapeños for a kick, or even some crumbled feta cheese for a tangy twist. Fresh herbs like cilantro or parsley can also enhance the flavor. Feel free to get creative and make it your own!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. How should I store and reheat leftover Honey Butter Skillet Corn?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>To store leftover Honey Butter Skillet Corn, let it cool completely and then transfer it to an airtight container. It can be kept in the refrigerator for up to 3 days. To reheat, simply warm it in a skillet over low heat, adding a little butter if needed to restore its creamy texture. Enjoy it as a quick side dish or a tasty snack!</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Get ready to savor the delightful sweetness of Honey Butter Skillet Corn! This dish is not just easy to whip up, but it also brings a warm, nostalgic feeling to your table. So gather your loved ones, enjoy every buttery bite, and let the simple joys of cooking fill your heart. Happy cooking!</p>\n",
